BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:86a0f656d1936eda@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART:20260921T130000Z
DTEND:20260921T150000Z
SUMMARY:INDIAN ARCHAEOLOGY
LOCATION:Conference Room II\, IIC main\, India International Centre\, 40 
 Max Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/indian-archaeology-151
DESCRIPTION:Prehistoric Vindhyan Childhoods: Investigating Rock Art as a 
 Knowledge System in Indian Prehistory\nSpeaker: Dr. Ajay Pratap is former
  Head and Professor\, Department of History\, Banaras Hindu University.\n
 Chair: K. N. Shrivastava\, Director\, IIC\nModerator: Pratap Bhanu Singh 
 Sengar\, former Director (Monuments) Archaeological Survey of India\nThe 
 emergence of an archaeology of childhood recognises the crucial roles of 
 women and children in prehistoric cultures and communities. The presentat
 ion explores their role as active users of visual symbolic representation
 \, as teachers and learners\, through rock art depicting self-images\, de
 signs\, narrative scenes\, line drawings and practice figures. It examine
 s rock art as a means of transmitting traditional knowledge\, aesthetics 
 and memory.\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/indian-archaeology-151
CATEGORIES:talk\,art\,heritage
END:VEVENT
