BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d67b93bbbd3be974@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Raj Se Swaraj Tak From Colonial Rule to Freedom- Through the Eyes
  of Shekhawati
LOCATION:Visual Arts Gallery\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New De
 lhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Exhibitions_Details
DESCRIPTION:To mark India’s 80th year of Independence\, MOHAR (Museum o
 f Heritage and Art at Ramgarh) presents “Raj Se Swaraj Tak”\, an imme
 rse eight-day journey of pre-independence and Post independence India in 
 the 1800s and 1900s\, through the discoveries in the Havelies of the Shek
 hawati Seths\, who created the magical frescoed region of Shekhawati\, ca
 lled the “Open-air Art gallery of Rajasthan”.\nThe exhibition and oth
 er events will showcase cultural narratives and lifestyles through the wa
 ll frescoes of Shekhawati\, the art and design influences\, belief system
 s\, religious and folk stories\, the British influence\, political art\, 
 lifestyle secrets\, architecture\, attire\, objects created or acquired b
 y the Shekhawati Seths - Art\, Media\, Manuscripts\, Telegrams\, Newspape
 rs\, Letters\, Maps\, spectacular oleographs\,\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.or
 g/Exhibitions_Details
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,history
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4aa9ae3b742b07d6@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Odyssey
LOCATION:Bikaner House\, Pandara Road\, India Gate\, New Delhi 110011
URL:https://bikanerhouse.rajasthan.gov.in/upcoming-events/2026/9
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Khushi Art his exhibition by Poonam Bhatnagar is
  about mythological characters\, world universes and landscapes as well a
 s an abstract series of geometry and symbolism in contemporary characters
 . Her exhibition of acrylics on canvas as well as drawings on paper creat
 ed in terms of Mythos accents and characters from Indian mythology. Her d
 etails\, her narrative and her compositional brilliance are a set of stor
 ies that transcend both time and tradition. As an artist she has been tra
 cing tradition in the old ideology of mythos and studying landscapes. She
  combines the lexicon of language with the concept of the rustic rhythms 
 of Indian identities in Mythos. This show is curated by Uma Nair.\n\nhttp
 s://bikanerhouse.rajasthan.gov.in/upcoming-events/2026/9
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art
END:VEVENT
