BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d4b9ed257d6b25c4@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:A Moment in the Monumental
LOCATION:Bikaner House\, Pandara Road\, India Gate\, New Delhi 110011
URL:https://bikanerhouse.rajasthan.gov.in/upcoming-events/2026/9
DESCRIPTION:Art Alive Gallery\, which was set up in New Delhi in 2001 and
  celebrates its silver anniversary in 2026. In arriving at this benchmark
 \, the gallery has played a critical role in taking Indian art forward wi
 th key exhibitions\, a vibrant publishing platform\, vital support for ar
 t events and collaborations\, and a diverse range of activities. Its rost
 er of artists has ranged from modern masters to senior and respected cont
 emporaries whose works it has exhibited\, including S.H. Raza\, M.F. Husa
 in\, Krishen Khanna\, Akbar Padamsee\, Anjolie Ela Menon\, K.G. Subramany
 an\, Satish Gujral\, Sakti Burman\, Senaka Senanayake\, K. Laxma Goud\, J
 ogen Chowdhury and Paritosh Sen on the one hand\, and Manu Parekh\, Madhv
 i Parekh\, Paresh Maity\, Jayasri Burman\, Arpana Caur\, Thota Vaikuntam 
 and Veer Munshi\, among others\, on the other hand these artists have bee
 n important contributors to the making of the Indian art story and Art Al
 ive features these and a whole host of other artists as part of its anniv
 ersary exhibition that is being curated to draw parallels that have exist
 ed in India’s art making practice since the very dawn of civilization. 
 The exhibition hopes to start conversations on the past\, present and fut
 ure of Indian art in engaging and meaningful ways.\n\nhttps://bikanerhous
 e.rajasthan.gov.in/upcoming-events/2026/9
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,heritage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fc0eb9065f6a995c@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:Nar Nari 2.0
LOCATION:Bikaner House\, Pandara Road\, India Gate\, New Delhi 110011
URL:https://bikanerhouse.rajasthan.gov.in/upcoming-events/2026/10
DESCRIPTION:Nar Nari 2.0 is a new and evolved body of work exploring the 
 eternal balance between masculine and feminine energies. The collection r
 eflects equality\, coexistence\, emotional strength\, and the idea that t
 wo contrasting forces together create wholeness. Rather than conflict\, t
 he works celebrate harmony between opposites—logic and intuition\, stru
 cture and softness\, earth and spirit. Mahesh Sharma is an Indian multidi
 sciplinary artist and designer known for his powerful fusion of fine art\
 , sculpture\, and collectible design. With over twenty-five years of crea
 tive experience\, his work spans exhibitions\, installations\, furniture-
 art\, and large-scale conceptual presentations in India and abroad. His a
 rtistic language is rooted in nature\, human psychology\, equality\, spir
 ituality\, and material transformation. Through painting\, sculpture\, an
 d mixed media\, Mahesh Sharma creates works that are both visually striki
 ng and philosophically layered. He is widely recognized for developing or
 iginal collections that merge art and function while maintaining a strong
  emotional and symbolic presence.\n\nhttps://bikanerhouse.rajasthan.gov.i
 n/upcoming-events/2026/10
